# Baker Hughes Weekly Rig Count API

A Flask REST API for serving rig count data from your Baker Hughes Weekly CSV file.

## Data Structure

Your CSV contains **20,297 rows** with these columns:

| Column | Description | Example Values |
|--------|-------------|----------------|
| `Country` | Country | UNITED STATES, CANADA |
| `County` | County name | BURLESON, LEE, CENTRAL SASKATCHEWAN |
| `Basin` | Basin name | Permian, Eagle Ford, Other |
| `GOM` | Gulf of Mexico flag | Yes, No |
| `DrillFor` | Target resource | Oil, Gas |
| `Location` | Location type | Land, Offshore |
| `State/Province` | State or province | TEXAS, SASKATCHEWAN |
| `Trajectory` | Well trajectory | Horizontal, Vertical |
| `Year` | Year | 2024, 2025 |
| `Month` | Month number | 1-12 |
| `US_PublishDate` | Publish date | 2024-08-23 |
| `Rig Count Value` | Rig count | 1, 2, 3... |

---

## Quick Start

### 1. Setup

```bash
# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv

# Activate it
# Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate
# Mac/Linux:
source venv/bin/activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 2. Add Your CSV File

Copy your `Baker_Hughes_Weekly.csv` into this directory (or set the path via environment variable):

```bash
# Windows
set CSV_PATH=C:\path\to\Baker_Hughes_Weekly.csv

# Mac/Linux
export CSV_PATH="/path/to/Baker_Hughes_Weekly.csv"
```

### 3. Run the API

```bash
python app.py
```

The API will be available at `http://localhost:5000`

---

## API Endpoints

### Core Data Endpoints

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `/` | GET | API documentation |
| `/health` | GET | Health check with data status |
| `/data` | GET | Get all data (paginated) |
| `/data/columns` | GET | List columns with metadata |
| `/data/summary` | GET | Summary statistics |
| `/data/filter` | GET | Filter by any column |
| `/data/latest` | GET | Most recent records |
| `/data/date-range` | GET | Filter by date range |

### Aggregation Endpoints

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `/aggregate/by-state` | GET | Rig counts by state/province |
| `/aggregate/by-basin` | GET | Rig counts by basin |
| `/aggregate/by-country` | GET | Rig counts by country |
| `/aggregate/by-date` | GET | Time series (total by date) |
| `/aggregate/time-series` | GET | Time series with grouping |

### Utility Endpoints

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `/unique/<column>` | GET | Unique values for a column |
| `/reload` | POST | Reload CSV from disk |

---

## Usage Examples

### Get All Data (Paginated)
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/data?page=1&per_page=50"
```

### Filter by State
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/data/filter?State/Province=TEXAS"
```

### Filter by Basin
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/data/filter?Basin=Permian"
```

### Filter by Drill Type (Oil vs Gas)
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/data/filter?DrillFor=Oil"
```

### Combined Filters
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/data/filter?Country=UNITED%20STATES&DrillFor=Oil&Trajectory=Horizontal"
```

### Get Latest Data (Most Recent Publish Date)
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/data/latest?n=50"
```

### Date Range Query
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/data/date-range?start=2024-01-01&end=2024-12-31"
```

### Rig Count by State (Latest Date)
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/aggregate/by-state?country=UNITED%20STATES"
```

### Rig Count by Basin (Specific Date)
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/aggregate/by-basin?date=2024-08-23&country=UNITED%20STATES"
```

### Time Series for Texas Oil Rigs
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/aggregate/by-date?state=TEXAS&drill_for=Oil"
```

### Time Series Grouped by Basin (US Only)
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/aggregate/time-series?group_by=Basin&country=UNITED%20STATES"
```

### Get All Unique Basins
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/unique/Basin"
```

### Get All Unique States
```bash
curl "http://localhost:5000/unique/State%2FProvince"
```

---

## Query Parameters

### Pagination & Sorting (all endpoints)

| Parameter | Default | Description |
|-----------|---------|-------------|
| `page` | 1 | Page number |
| `per_page` | 100 | Results per page (max: 1000) |
| `sort_by` | US_PublishDate | Column to sort by |
| `sort_order` | desc | `asc` or `desc` |

### Filter Operators

| Operator | Example | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `=` | `State/Province=TEXAS` | Exact match |
| `*...*` | `Basin=*Permian*` | Contains |
| `>` | `Rig Count Value=>10` | Greater than |
| `<` | `Year=<2025` | Less than |
| `>=` | `Month=>=6` | Greater than or equal |
| `<=` | `Month=<=12` | Less than or equal |

---

## Configuration

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `CSV_PATH` | `Baker_Hughes_Weekly.csv` | Path to CSV file |
| `PORT` | `5000` | Server port |
| `API_KEY` | None | Optional API key |
| `FLASK_DEBUG` | `False` | Enable debug mode |

### Enable API Key Protection

```bash
export API_KEY="your-secret-key-here"
```

Then include in requests:
```bash
curl -H "X-API-Key: your-secret-key-here" "http://localhost:5000/data"
```

---

## Deployment Options

### Local Production (Gunicorn)
```bash
gunicorn -w 4 -b 0.0.0.0:5000 app:app
```

### Railway
1. Push to GitHub
2. Connect Railway to your repo
3. Set `CSV_PATH` environment variable
4. Deploy

### Docker
```dockerfile
FROM python:3.11-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY requirements.txt .
RUN pip install -r requirements.txt
COPY . .
CMD ["gunicorn", "-w", "4", "-b", "0.0.0.0:5000", "app:app"]
```

---

## Excel / Power Query Integration

```m
let
    Source = Json.Document(Web.Contents("http://localhost:5000/aggregate/by-date?country=UNITED STATES")),
    data = Source[data],
    toTable = Table.FromList(data, Splitter.SplitByNothing(), null, null, ExtraValues.Error),
    expanded = Table.ExpandRecordColumn(toTable, "Column1", {"US_PublishDate", "Rig Count Value"})
in
    expanded
```

---

## Response Format

All endpoints return JSON:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "Country": "UNITED STATES",
      "State/Province": "TEXAS",
      "Basin": "Permian",
      "DrillFor": "Oil",
      "Rig Count Value": 5,
      "US_PublishDate": "2024-08-23"
    }
  ],
  "pagination": {
    "page": 1,
    "per_page": 100,
    "total": 20297,
    "total_pages": 203,
    "has_next": true
  }
}
```